# The development host's three keys (T-485, row N161; decision record T-484, section 6, "Where each key lives").
# They live in the vault Crow-Agents, which one 1Password service account reads and nothing else; this is the only
# references file that may name that vault, and it may name no other (scripts/secrets/refs.mjs, VAULTS).
# On the development host, as the session user:
#   infra/dev-host/with-keys.sh --yes node infra/party/up.mjs --role buyer --run <id> --yes
# On Rafa's own Mac, for the team test of move step 4, with the Claude desktop app quit:
#   op run --env-file=config/secrets/dev-host.refs -- node infra/party/team-test.mjs make --run <id>
#
# The agents' GitHub account: a classic token with the repo scope and without workflow, 90 days.
CROW_AGENTS_GITHUB_TOKEN=op://crow-agents/devhost-agents-github/credential
# The crow-parties team at DigitalOcean: Droplets create, read and delete; tags create and read; SSH keys read;
# images read; 90 days. doctl reads the same name.
DIGITALOCEAN_ACCESS_TOKEN=op://crow-agents/devhost-parties-digitalocean/credential
# The simulated parties' model key, from the Anthropic workspace crow-parties with its monthly spend limit.
HOLDBACK_PARTY_ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=op://crow-agents/devhost-parties-anthropic/credential
